WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:03.791
[Rogue] <i>Previously on</i> X-Men...

2
00:00:03.792 --> 00:00:05.832
<i>Just hard to believe that we might</i>

3
00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:08.832
finally be able to punch our ticket home.

4
00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:10.833
- [fire crackling]
- What is awaiting you there?

5
00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:15.208
[Rogue] It's more about
what's not waiting for me.

6
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.375
<i>Someone... I lost.</i>

7
00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:22.500
<i>Someone... special.</i>

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.250
[En Sabah Nur] <i>Everyone
I have ever known. I've lost.</i>

9
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.875
<i>Love is pain.</i>

10
00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:37.000
[Rogue] <i>And the only thing
that makes life worth living...</i>

11
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.791
[chuckles softly] And there's the rub.

12
00:00:40.792 --> 00:00:44.332
I do hope you get to
experience it one day.

13
00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:46.167
For all our sakes.

14
00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:49.292
[♪ theme music playing]

15
00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:54.500
[screaming]

16
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

17
00:01:04.292 --> 00:01:06.542
How? How could this be?

18
00:02:26.292 --> 00:02:28.625
[fireworks exploding]

19
00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:36.332
[♪ enchanting music playing]

20
00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:38.583
[inhales. exhales]

21
00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:15.250
[sighs]

22
00:03:25.458 --> 00:03:27.082
Remember. <i>chère...</i>

23
00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:29.541
- [♪ music ends abruptly]
- Oh.

24
00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.875
...some things be deeper than skin.

25
00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:34.375
[gasps]

26
00:03:35.292 --> 00:03:37.333
[screaming in pain]

27
00:03:37.958 --> 00:03:41.542
[screaming. panting]

28
00:03:48.958 --> 00:03:51.916
Hold on. Jean.
I thought we said no powers.

29
00:03:51.917 --> 00:03:54.541
It's not my fault
that your tells are so obvious.

30
00:03:54.542 --> 00:03:57.999
Your turn. Professor. Are you in or out?

31
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.916
[sighs] Sadly. [chuckles] I must fold.

32
00:04:00.917 --> 00:04:05.291
Well. that leaves myself
<i>und</i> the very quiet Dr. McCoy.

33
00:04:05.292 --> 00:04:07.458
Don't let him sucker you in. Beast.

34
00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:10.083
Aces over eights.

35
00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:14.667
The Dead Man's Hand.
Fortunately. mine is much livelier.

36
00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:17.583
Three threes
from your fellow friend in blue.

37
00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:20.791
- [gasps]
- [Jean chuckles] Way to go. Beast.

38
00:04:20.792 --> 00:04:23.374
[Nightcrawler] At least tell me
how you broke my streak.

39
00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:26.291
"Life is not always
a matter of holding good cards.

40
00:04:26.292 --> 00:04:29.124
but sometimes playing a poor hand well."

41
00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:31.166
- Jack London.
- [Cyclops] Yeah. yeah.

42
00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:34.333
- Save it for the book club.
- [all laughing]

43
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:39.208
- [sighs]
- Is everything all right. my child?

44
00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.541
Just glad to be among friends.

45
00:04:42.542 --> 00:04:44.917
[alarm blaring]

46
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.917
Now. who pulled the fire alarm?

47
00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:53.457
An unidentified military bomber.
heavily armed with psionic jammers.

48
00:04:53.458 --> 00:04:57.791
Unidentified aircraft.
you are trespassing private airspace.

49
00:04:57.792 --> 00:04:59.250
Please state your purpose.

50
00:05:07.917 --> 00:05:11.874
[Beast] <i>Surely only a madman
would try and breach our EMP field.</i>

51
00:05:11.875 --> 00:05:14.374
[Professor X] This is your final warning.

52
00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:15.875
Alter course immediately.

53
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.541
Hank. prepare to engage.

54
00:05:20.542 --> 00:05:23.457
Wait! I can sense a mind
through the jammers.

55
00:05:23.458 --> 00:05:24.999
Presence drawn to...

56
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.375
me and Scott?

57
00:05:32.125 --> 00:05:33.707
Nathan?

58
00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:35.000
Oh. dear.

59
00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:40.333
- Hi guys. we need help.
- We're coming in for a landing.

60
00:05:52.375 --> 00:05:55.125
[♪ dramatic music playing]

61
00:06:05.417 --> 00:06:07.291
- Son.
- [Jean] Nathan.

62
00:06:07.292 --> 00:06:10.207
It's. um... good to see you again.

63
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:13.082
Yeah. there's a lot to catch up on.

64
00:06:13.083 --> 00:06:15.333
Right now. there's been a murder.

65
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.917
And that's not even the bad news.

66
00:06:20.708 --> 00:06:21.750
Rogue...

67
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:27.208
- There's something you need to see.
- [sighs]

68
00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:46.457
[Psylocke] Apocalypse overestimated
his ability to control

69
00:06:46.458 --> 00:06:49.458
a Horseman who's been
resurrected from the grave.

70
00:06:51.292 --> 00:06:56.124
So. what you're saying is.
whatever has been brought back

71
00:06:56.125 --> 00:06:58.874
might not really be Remy?

72
00:06:58.875 --> 00:07:00.666
We'll know when we find him.

73
00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:04.416
Which is why we need you
to use Cerebro to do so.

74
00:07:04.417 --> 00:07:08.541
No way we're helping you
add Gambit to your posse's dirty hitlist!

75
00:07:08.542 --> 00:07:10.624
This isn't about killing him.

76
00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:13.416
It's about undoing the evil in him.

77
00:07:13.417 --> 00:07:17.500
Rogue. years ago. you freed me
from Apocalypse's corruption.

78
00:07:18.042 --> 00:07:19.624
[Psylocke] We sneak you in close

79
00:07:19.625 --> 00:07:22.707
so you can use your gifts
to restore Gambit's soul.

80
00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:26.457
But how do we know
his soul is there to restore?

81
00:07:26.458 --> 00:07:28.249
We have to believe

82
00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.582
that a part of Gambit endures.

83
00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:34.832
Such questions will have to wait
until we've recovered him.

84
00:07:34.833 --> 00:07:36.707
That mean we have a deal. Chuck?

85
00:07:36.708 --> 00:07:41.207
On one condition.
this is our rescue mission.

86
00:07:41.208 --> 00:07:43.500
Brute tactics will not be tolerated.

87
00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:45.541
Gambit's not himself.

88
00:07:45.542 --> 00:07:48.917
We're just here to make sure
he doesn't put anyone else in danger.

89
00:07:52.208 --> 00:07:54.416
[Rogue] Gambit's alive?

90
00:07:54.417 --> 00:07:56.582
And he's killed Apocalypse?

91
00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:59.332
We have witnessed our share or miracles.

92
00:07:59.333 --> 00:08:00.499
Huh.

93
00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.874
My daddy used to say. a miracle is just

94
00:08:02.875 --> 00:08:05.417
wrapping paper for the next tragedy.

95
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:10.542
Rogue. this is not the time
for your colorful lamentations.

96
00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.167
Remy is back.

97
00:08:15.625 --> 00:08:17.125
I know. Kurt. I know.

98
00:08:17.958 --> 00:08:20.333
And I'm afraid of what that means.

99
00:08:21.917 --> 00:08:24.166
Everything will be fine. sister.

100
00:08:24.167 --> 00:08:25.833
I promise.

101
00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:32.374
We've made some updates. We call it...

102
00:08:32.375 --> 00:08:34.082
Cerebra.

103
00:08:34.083 --> 00:08:35.707
[Professor X] If Gambit is out there.

104
00:08:35.708 --> 00:08:37.792
this will help me find him.

105
00:08:44.208 --> 00:08:46.458
[♪ captivating music playing]

106
00:08:50.583 --> 00:08:52.375
[indistinct chatter]

107
00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:59.582
Mighty untoward.
peekin' at another man's cards.

108
00:08:59.583 --> 00:09:02.083
[gasps. groans]

109
00:09:04.417 --> 00:09:06.000
[Professor X panting]

110
00:09:06.958 --> 00:09:08.833
Professor. did you find him?

111
00:09:10.958 --> 00:09:12.999
[Professor X] I fear there's

112
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.750
more to this darkness
than we have yet to understand.

113
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.667
Just tell us where he's gone.

114
00:09:22.542 --> 00:09:24.417
He's gone home.

115
00:09:50.333 --> 00:09:53.582
Evenin'. Robert. What's goin' on?

116
00:09:53.583 --> 00:09:55.457
[Robert] You tell me. Bella Donna.

117
00:09:55.458 --> 00:09:57.832
It's you who invited us here. no?

118
00:09:57.833 --> 00:09:59.624
Don't be stupid.

119
00:09:59.625 --> 00:10:02.957
Why would I send myself this invitation?

120
00:10:02.958 --> 00:10:04.833
[Gambit] The invitations were mine.

121
00:10:05.792 --> 00:10:08.375
- [♪ dramatic music playing]
- [all gasping]

122
00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:18.582
Surprised to see me?

123
00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:20.458
I know I am.

124
00:10:22.375 --> 00:10:24.041
Remy? But you...

125
00:10:24.042 --> 00:10:28.583
Aw. <i>petite</i>. you don't look so happy
to see your thieving ex.

126
00:10:29.958 --> 00:10:32.250
What the hell happened to you?

127
00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.332
What happened. big brother?

128
00:10:35.333 --> 00:10:38.208
- For starters. I died.
- [gasps]

129
00:10:39.083 --> 00:10:41.624
Then the Devil snatched me
out of the grave.

130
00:10:41.625 --> 00:10:44.041
A real bad customer.

131
00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:46.042
[all gasping]

132
00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.624
Remy. please.

133
00:10:52.625 --> 00:10:54.292
[Gambit] Don't be scared. <i>chérie.</i>

134
00:10:54.792 --> 00:10:57.666
Death is evolution.

135
00:10:57.667 --> 00:10:59.958
[all groaning]

136
00:11:01.125 --> 00:11:03.917
[all screaming]

137
00:11:15.375 --> 00:11:17.333
[Jubilee] Hey. I...

138
00:11:17.458 --> 00:11:21.958
I'm sorry. I know this will be hard.
Facing Gambit.

139
00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.457
Got nothing to be sorry for. sugar.

140
00:11:25.458 --> 00:11:28.249
Remy's weighing on all our hearts.

141
00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:31.416
Can't let regret make it feel heavier.

142
00:11:31.417 --> 00:11:35.874
Heck. probably best
X-Force stayed clear of Remy. anyhow.

143
00:11:35.875 --> 00:11:38.541
Sure. they can be a little intense.

144
00:11:38.542 --> 00:11:41.249
But tracking Apocalypse
these past few months.

145
00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.666
I've learned that
you can't shut your heart off.

146
00:11:44.667 --> 00:11:47.667
'Cause that's the thing
that's gonna get you through this.

147
00:11:54.042 --> 00:11:56.000
Family reunion time already?

148
00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:59.499
We wanted to check in...

149
00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:01.375
See how you're holding up.

150
00:12:05.333 --> 00:12:08.916
It must have been strange.
finding Apocalypse.

151
00:12:08.917 --> 00:12:12.042
Not exactly how I'd pictured my destiny.

152
00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.416
Why didn't you tell us. Nathan?

153
00:12:16.417 --> 00:12:18.499
That you'd met us as a boy?

154
00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.874
Why not reach out when we got back?

155
00:12:20.875 --> 00:12:23.374
Time would have ripped us apart again.

156
00:12:23.375 --> 00:12:24.750
like it always does.

157
00:12:26.083 --> 00:12:28.916
Well. I've about had my fill
of what happened yesterday.

158
00:12:28.917 --> 00:12:30.999
or could tomorrow.

159
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.207
For once. son.

160
00:12:32.208 --> 00:12:34.833
can we focus on what we could be today?

161
00:12:36.208 --> 00:12:37.208
[Jean] A family.

162
00:12:42.083 --> 00:12:44.291
We scout for Gambit quick and quiet.

163
00:12:44.292 --> 00:12:47.667
unless we want X-Factor
and their Mech-Sentinels on our butts.

164
00:12:48.333 --> 00:12:51.707
No way Val Cooper
and her government stooges found us.

165
00:12:51.708 --> 00:12:54.874
I sense no Mech-Sentinel pilots outside.
but I do sense--

166
00:12:54.875 --> 00:12:58.917
A swarm of black holes
where minds and souls should be.

167
00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.207
- [missile whistles]
- [explosion]

168
00:13:06.208 --> 00:13:07.749
[all grunting]

169
00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:10.375
[♪ dramatic music playing]

170
00:13:15.792 --> 00:13:17.250
[Bella Donna grunting]

171
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.041
Bella Donna? Robert?

172
00:13:22.042 --> 00:13:23.541
What's he done to ya?

173
00:13:23.542 --> 00:13:24.874
Skip the shock and awe.

174
00:13:24.875 --> 00:13:26.375
Find Gambit. Now!

175
00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.833
[all grunting]

176
00:13:32.708 --> 00:13:35.167
- [gasps]
- [groans]

177
00:13:36.167 --> 00:13:37.458
[grunting]

178
00:13:40.875 --> 00:13:42.250
[gasps]

179
00:13:47.542 --> 00:13:48.958
[Rogue grunts]

180
00:13:54.542 --> 00:13:55.542
Remy?

181
00:13:56.792 --> 00:13:59.667
Remy. it's me. It's Rogue.

182
00:14:02.917 --> 00:14:05.250
Apocalypse poisoned your mind.

183
00:14:05.792 --> 00:14:07.250
I can help you.

184
00:14:07.792 --> 00:14:09.375
Just trust me.

185
00:14:13.667 --> 00:14:14.667
[Gambit] You know...

186
00:14:16.042 --> 00:14:19.417
life does flash before our eyes
when we die.

187
00:14:20.583 --> 00:14:22.833
[♪ melancholy music playing]

188
00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:29.500
And when I died...

189
00:14:30.917 --> 00:14:32.750
all I saw...

190
00:14:33.583 --> 00:14:34.708
was you.

191
00:14:38.417 --> 00:14:39.917
[gasps]

192
00:14:43.417 --> 00:14:45.249
What's wrong?

193
00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:47.292
That ain't possible.

194
00:14:47.917 --> 00:14:49.582
Warned you. <i>chère.</i>

195
00:14:49.583 --> 00:14:52.875
Some things. they be deeper than skin.

196
00:14:54.333 --> 00:14:55.375
Sleep.

197
00:14:56.208 --> 00:14:57.458
[gasps]

198
00:14:59.458 --> 00:15:02.041
[Jean] <i>X-Men.
I've lost contact with Rogue.</i>

199
00:15:02.042 --> 00:15:04.541
[both grunting]

200
00:15:04.542 --> 00:15:05.583
I'm on it!

201
00:15:09.417 --> 00:15:11.708
Put her down. Remy. You are not yourself.

202
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.625
[grunts]

203
00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:19.042
[groaning]

204
00:15:20.292 --> 00:15:23.000
Now. neither are you. <i>mon ami.</i>

205
00:15:25.292 --> 00:15:28.250
- [♪ dramatic music playing]
- [tires screeching]

206
00:15:29.708 --> 00:15:31.417
[explosions]

207
00:15:32.167 --> 00:15:34.333
[all grunting]

208
00:15:43.208 --> 00:15:44.999
The wings are coming off.

209
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.332
We gotta go after Gambit.

210
00:15:46.333 --> 00:15:48.874
No. we need every telekinetic
landing this plane

211
00:15:48.875 --> 00:15:50.625
- or we're all toast.
- [straining]

212
00:15:51.958 --> 00:15:53.208
[straining]

213
00:15:55.708 --> 00:15:58.416
We can do this. son. together.

214
00:15:58.417 --> 00:16:00.875
[both grunting]

215
00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.417
[screaming]

216
00:16:09.917 --> 00:16:12.457
- [panting]
- [groaning]

217
00:16:12.458 --> 00:16:13.792
[screaming]

218
00:16:19.583 --> 00:16:23.750
{\an8}[reporter] <i>The Pentagon has confirmed
the plane belonged to X-Force.</i>

219
00:16:23.875 --> 00:16:28.791
{\an8}<i>They've yet to say if this was
a failed terrorist attack or a crash.</i>

220
00:16:28.792 --> 00:16:32.749
News was spooking the kids.
so I put on <i>The Exorcist.</i>

221
00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:35.041
Didn't get these back
just to play gym coach

222
00:16:35.042 --> 00:16:37.582
while Jean and the others
are blown out of the sky.

223
00:16:37.583 --> 00:16:39.875
The school will be safe with Colossus.

224
00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.957
Right now. our family needs us.

225
00:16:42.958 --> 00:16:45.416
And X-Men fight for their own.

226
00:16:45.417 --> 00:16:46.417
Let's move.

227
00:16:47.917 --> 00:16:49.708
[gasps]

228
00:16:58.083 --> 00:17:00.750
Kurt. what's he done to you?

229
00:17:01.625 --> 00:17:05.374
Time to rise. sister. Dinner is served.

230
00:17:05.375 --> 00:17:07.792
And you are the guest of honor.

231
00:17:08.542 --> 00:17:10.750
[♪ slow music playing]

232
00:17:18.792 --> 00:17:20.292
Evenin'. <i>chère.</i>

233
00:17:33.333 --> 00:17:36.749
[chuckles] Siccing your brainwashed
ex on me

234
00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:40.291
is a mighty bold way
to ask a lady out to dinner.

235
00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:44.000
You did always like my unorthodox flair.

236
00:17:46.667 --> 00:17:48.332
Gambit never woulda dreamed

237
00:17:48.333 --> 00:17:51.332
you'd be working with the merc
hunting me down. neither.

238
00:17:51.333 --> 00:17:54.166
Cable? No. Remy.

239
00:17:54.167 --> 00:17:56.042
We were tryin' to save you.

240
00:17:56.708 --> 00:17:57.916
[sighs]

241
00:17:57.917 --> 00:18:00.250
I thought I could.

242
00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:06.457
World's been conspiring
to keep us apart for so long. <i>chère.</i>

243
00:18:06.458 --> 00:18:09.416
We both learned to expect the worst.

244
00:18:09.417 --> 00:18:13.791
But now. now we've been dealt
a whole new hand.

245
00:18:13.792 --> 00:18:17.916
That gap between the man I was
and the one you want

246
00:18:17.917 --> 00:18:19.458
is finally gone.

247
00:18:20.375 --> 00:18:23.124
Or at least. it can be.

248
00:18:23.125 --> 00:18:26.124
This is just so strange.

249
00:18:26.125 --> 00:18:31.041
Getting you back. why.
is all I ever dreamed of.

250
00:18:31.042 --> 00:18:34.249
But now. you're here and...

251
00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.792
I don't know if I should be relieved...

252
00:18:37.333 --> 00:18:38.832
or scared.

253
00:18:38.833 --> 00:18:41.792
I ain't crawled outta my grave
to repeat regrets.

254
00:18:42.542 --> 00:18:44.125
This is our second chance.

255
00:18:44.708 --> 00:18:47.333
So. no more holding
my cards close to my chest.

256
00:18:48.083 --> 00:18:49.916
So. here they are. <i>belle.</i>

257
00:18:49.917 --> 00:18:53.124
I learned Apocalypse
ain't no different than us.

258
00:18:53.125 --> 00:18:56.166
<i>He had a love that broke his heart too.</i>

259
00:18:56.167 --> 00:18:59.541
<i>A priestess of ancient Egypt courted him.</i>

260
00:18:59.542 --> 00:19:03.083
<i>convinced him to give her
a piece of his power...</i>

261
00:19:09.333 --> 00:19:11.792
[exclaiming in pain]

262
00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:17.041
[Gambit] <i>Only to betray him.</i>

263
00:19:17.042 --> 00:19:21.125
<i>A trap she laid to seek revenge
for what he did to her people.</i>

264
00:19:22.708 --> 00:19:24.000
[groans]

265
00:19:25.042 --> 00:19:29.124
She done run away with it.
right here to the bayou.

266
00:19:29.125 --> 00:19:32.542
Locals know her as the X-Ternal.

267
00:19:33.708 --> 00:19:36.916
Her relic will make you immortal like me.

268
00:19:36.917 --> 00:19:41.625
It'll bind us together forever.
husband and wife.

269
00:19:42.417 --> 00:19:47.042
And then nothin'. not even death
ever keep us apart again.

270
00:19:48.917 --> 00:19:50.041
[sighs wearily]

271
00:19:50.042 --> 00:19:53.791
How do I know I can trust you?

272
00:19:53.792 --> 00:19:56.167
'Cause I'm offering us a second chance.

273
00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.957
You gotta believe in me.

274
00:19:58.958 --> 00:20:00.625
Believe in us. <i>chère.</i>

275
00:20:03.708 --> 00:20:05.792
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

276
00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:22.792
[distant whoosh]

277
00:20:24.542 --> 00:20:28.458
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

278
00:20:46.583 --> 00:20:48.583
- [squelching]
- [gasps]

279
00:20:51.792 --> 00:20:56.167
The Assassins Guild calls upon
its covenant with the X-Ternal.

280
00:20:57.375 --> 00:21:00.167
Let this tribute awake you from your sleep

281
00:21:00.583 --> 00:21:02.375
and summon you forth...

282
00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:06.499
[rumbling]

283
00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.292
- [thunderclap]
- [gasps]

284
00:21:09.375 --> 00:21:11.833
[♪ dramatic music playing]

285
00:21:12.958 --> 00:21:15.292
[thunderclap]

286
00:21:17.958 --> 00:21:21.250
Who dares disturb my slumber?

287
00:21:22.292 --> 00:21:25.832
- <i>C'est moi</i>.
- [External] Remy LeBeau.

288
00:21:25.833 --> 00:21:29.207
This is unexpected.

289
00:21:29.208 --> 00:21:32.666
You have become stained and defiled.

290
00:21:32.667 --> 00:21:34.500
What is it that you seek?

291
00:21:39.917 --> 00:21:41.832
[laughs maniacally]

292
00:21:41.833 --> 00:21:45.832
This is forged
from the very fires of creation.

293
00:21:45.833 --> 00:21:48.249
given to me by Apocalypse.

294
00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.708
'Fraid not. it belongs to me.

295
00:21:50.833 --> 00:21:53.541
You stole it from my predecessor.

296
00:21:53.542 --> 00:21:56.375
You dare to defy me?

297
00:21:57.583 --> 00:22:01.749
I have stood by the Devil's side
and glimpsed his dark intents.

298
00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:05.874
I will not indulge a scoundrel
to entertain his--

299
00:22:05.875 --> 00:22:08.624
- [squelching]
- [gasps. groans]

300
00:22:08.625 --> 00:22:11.125
Sorry. gotta cut this game short.

301
00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:14.916
What goes around. come around.

302
00:22:14.917 --> 00:22:16.916
Remy. no!

303
00:22:16.917 --> 00:22:18.791
[sighs] What did you do?

304
00:22:18.792 --> 00:22:20.250
[Gambit] Going all in. <i>chère.</i>

305
00:22:20.792 --> 00:22:21.833
You ready?

306
00:22:39.792 --> 00:22:42.083
Gambit. we don't want to fight you.

307
00:22:42.708 --> 00:22:44.125
But we will.

308
00:22:45.333 --> 00:22:47.250
Stand down. Now.

309
00:22:48.083 --> 00:22:49.374
Remy. please.

310
00:22:49.375 --> 00:22:52.249
If that your bet. <i>mes amis</i>. I call.

311
00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:55.375
[all yelling]

312
00:23:01.208 --> 00:23:05.000
Tides. rise and help cleanse
this foul ritual.

313
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:09.749
[all gasping. coughing]

314
00:23:09.750 --> 00:23:11.083
[grunting]

315
00:23:13.167 --> 00:23:14.375
[grunting]

316
00:23:16.292 --> 00:23:18.333
[yelling. groaning]

317
00:23:21.875 --> 00:23:24.625
[all groaning]

318
00:23:28.375 --> 00:23:30.207
[Jubilee screaming]

319
00:23:30.208 --> 00:23:32.957
[all screaming]

320
00:23:32.958 --> 00:23:35.917
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

321
00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:40.917
[groaning. screaming in pain]

322
00:23:44.375 --> 00:23:47.708
[Professor X] <i>Remy.
it's time to end this madness.</i>

323
00:23:49.542 --> 00:23:50.917
[grunts]

324
00:23:53.167 --> 00:23:54.708
[groans]

325
00:24:01.833 --> 00:24:04.000
[Professor X]
<i>In the battlefield of the mind.</i>

326
00:24:04.583 --> 00:24:06.582
my will shall prevail.

327
00:24:06.583 --> 00:24:09.083
Now this be an unexpected delight.

328
00:24:14.333 --> 00:24:17.250
[groans. screams]

329
00:24:18.292 --> 00:24:22.292
Where was this will back in Genosha
when Gambit needed it?

330
00:24:25.208 --> 00:24:28.082
As Jean once used the power of the Phoenix

331
00:24:28.083 --> 00:24:30.332
to bind the M'kraan Crystal.

332
00:24:30.333 --> 00:24:32.666
I now bind you with the power of--

333
00:24:32.667 --> 00:24:34.417
[Professor X groans]

334
00:24:36.083 --> 00:24:38.708
[grunting]

335
00:24:44.792 --> 00:24:46.333
[both grunting]

336
00:24:51.250 --> 00:24:53.208
[Professor X exclaiming in pain]

337
00:24:55.667 --> 00:24:57.917
- [grunts]
- [gasps]

338
00:24:59.292 --> 00:25:01.707
- [gasps]
- Remy!

339
00:25:01.708 --> 00:25:03.791
If you can hear me.

340
00:25:03.792 --> 00:25:05.542
- come back to me!
- [exclaiming in pain]

341
00:25:06.375 --> 00:25:07.832
[Gambit] Professor.

342
00:25:07.833 --> 00:25:10.208
Help me. please!

343
00:25:15.500 --> 00:25:17.374
[grunting]

344
00:25:17.375 --> 00:25:18.708
Everyone. close your eyes!

345
00:25:24.958 --> 00:25:28.292
X-Force. Gambit's exposed.
It's time to make our move.

346
00:25:29.625 --> 00:25:31.124
Nathan. no!

347
00:25:31.125 --> 00:25:33.957
- [all gasping]
- We don't want to hurt you.

348
00:25:33.958 --> 00:25:35.999
but be certain that we will.

349
00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:37.374
Cable. what gives?

350
00:25:37.375 --> 00:25:40.999
Sorry. kiddo. Had to play nice
to get close enough for the kill.

351
00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:43.457
Nathan. do not make me
take over your mind.

352
00:25:43.458 --> 00:25:47.042
Apocalypse is in there.
and it's my destiny to kill him.

353
00:25:47.667 --> 00:25:49.292
[gasps]

354
00:25:51.625 --> 00:25:53.916
After all this time.

355
00:25:53.917 --> 00:25:58.624
the teacher has still learned nothing.

356
00:25:58.625 --> 00:26:01.374
You... You're alive.

357
00:26:01.375 --> 00:26:03.292
In here? How?

358
00:26:04.250 --> 00:26:08.166
I would have thought.
after your beloved Magnus.

359
00:26:08.167 --> 00:26:11.457
you might have finally understood.

360
00:26:11.458 --> 00:26:14.332
I always survive!

361
00:26:14.333 --> 00:26:16.583
[♪ dramatic music playing]

362
00:26:19.208 --> 00:26:20.208
[groans]

363
00:26:25.583 --> 00:26:27.042
[groans] Professor!

364
00:26:28.167 --> 00:26:30.000
- [Professor X exclaiming in pain]
- [groans]

365
00:26:51.417 --> 00:26:53.000
[yelling]

366
00:26:54.542 --> 00:26:55.625
Remy!

367
00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:07.292
[♪ dramatic music continues]

368
00:27:11.250 --> 00:27:13.750
Come on. sugar!

369
00:27:15.042 --> 00:27:18.917
[groaning. panting]

370
00:27:19.750 --> 00:27:21.542
[gasps]

371
00:27:22.250 --> 00:27:24.000
[yelling]

372
00:27:33.208 --> 00:27:35.917
[groans. gasps]

373
00:27:46.167 --> 00:27:48.541
[Professor X] <i>X-Men. we must retreat. now!</i>

374
00:27:48.542 --> 00:27:49.958
Kurt. you're back with us?

375
00:27:52.250 --> 00:27:53.875
[grunts]

376
00:27:58.583 --> 00:27:59.667
[grunts]

377
00:28:02.250 --> 00:28:05.249
[machine beeping]

378
00:28:05.250 --> 00:28:06.832
[Professor X] His vitals are faint.

379
00:28:06.833 --> 00:28:10.083
but his neural activity... most strange.

380
00:28:11.708 --> 00:28:16.583
Apocalypse will not stay contained
inside Remy's consciousness much longer.

381
00:28:17.542 --> 00:28:19.582
If we do not move quickly.

382
00:28:19.583 --> 00:28:21.583
he will take him over for good.

383
00:28:24.708 --> 00:28:26.333
[Rogue] I've got you. sugar.

384
00:28:27.708 --> 00:28:29.125
I won't lose you.

385
00:28:30.750 --> 00:28:32.042
Not again.

386
00:28:47.458 --> 00:28:49.624
[Warren] Your honeypot didn't work.

387
00:28:49.625 --> 00:28:50.708
[growls softly]

388
00:28:51.125 --> 00:28:52.374
Enough. Warren.

389
00:28:52.375 --> 00:28:54.666
- It's time to regroup.
- With whom?

390
00:28:54.667 --> 00:28:56.332
It's just us three now.

391
00:28:56.333 --> 00:28:58.458
- [explosion]
- [all gasp]

392
00:29:05.708 --> 00:29:08.499
[Nathan chuckles] If you think
you're taking us in.

393
00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:11.083
you're in for a surprise. pal.

394
00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:13.292
Hey. chief.

395
00:29:17.458 --> 00:29:19.333
You're not the ones we're after.

396
00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:24.375
{\an8}What do you say to both of us
getting what we want?

397
00:29:25.305 --> 00:30:25.205
